# cheat — personal reference tool

## Lookup
    cheat <sheet>                    # view a sheet (personal takes precedence)
    cheat <sheet> --tag=community    # explicitly view the community version
    cheat <sheet> --tag=personal     # explicitly view your personal version
    cheat -l                         # list all sheets
    cheat -l --tag=personal          # list only personal sheets

## Editing
    cheat -e <sheet>                 # create or edit a personal sheet

## Sheet strategy

Personal sheets override community sheets of the same name — but community
isn't gone, just deprioritised. Use `--tag=community` to reach it.

Good personal sheet = only what's yours: your workflow, your config choices,
things you'd otherwise forget. Don't duplicate community content. Signpost it:

    # Standard reference: cheat <tool> --tag=community

For tools you rarely touch personally, skip the personal sheet entirely
and let the community version serve.
